! C22-6578 PROBLEM 2.8, "PURCHASING LIST ARITHMETIC", printed pp.20-21
! (PDF 21-22), read in the ink (and at 170 dpi).
!
! >>> TRANSCRIBED AND ASSEMBLED.  NOT REGISTERED AS A RUN.  Until
! >>> 2026-11-16 the model refused the decimal add (OP at "+(D, 48, 8)",
! >>> half-word 2006) and the program did not halt (step cap, PC 2020,
! >>> inside KOMF).  <<<
!
! 2026-11-16, G2.3 stage 1 (decimal +, L, ST, M+ built): RUN WITH ASM=strap2
! (strap_asm gets the decimal DDs wrong, below), STEPS=3000.  OBSERVED:
!  * product 1's F field (word 1203's low 32 bits) is (16)03064941 where
!    it was (16)00004941: digits 3 and 6 in zone-0 bytes, "36" -- the
!    total the program AS PRINTED computes from this data, traced by hand
!    before the run: "+(D,48,8)" is signed, so E's last byte is a sign
!    byte, E is read as +00012 and added three times.  Not 375: see the
!    signed/unsigned reading below.
!  * product 2's F field is never written: the run is still at the step
!    cap, PC 2022, in the KOMF loop.  NOT TRACED: whether KOMF's
!    KF(BU,24)(V+I) against the TESTW accumulator can find this deck's
!    field boundary at all is the open question (docs/NEXT.md G2.3).
! So the decimal arithmetic the program reaches runs, and the run is not
! registered: there is no halt to pin and the loop is not understood.
!
! THE TWO BLANK F SUBFIELDS were one "(IQSQ)DD(BU,96,8)" each until
! 2026-11-16; STRAP II refuses it ("FIELD LENGTH GREATER THAN 64",
! C22-6531's limit), so each is two 48-bit DDs.  Same bits; the data are
! the deck's, not the page's.
!
!   "A purchasing list consists of a string of fields, each of which
!   has the following structure:  | A | B | C | D | E | F | G |
!   Subfield A is an eight-bit byte consisting of 1's.
!   Subfield B has two 8-bit bytes (item no.).
!   Subfield C has six 8-bit bytes (coded name of product).
!   Subfield D has three 8-bit bytes, and contains the number of units
!     of the product desired in decimal (DU, 24, 8).
!   Subfield E has six 8-bit bytes, and contains the unit price in
!     cents of the product in decimal (DU, 48, 8).
!   Subfield F has 12 8-bit bytes, and is blank (to be the total price
!     field).
!   Subfield G is an unknown number of 8-bit bytes.  It contains the
!     remarks concerning the product and/or the entire purchase.  The
!     first three 8-bit bytes of the subfield G in the last "product
!     field" contains the 8-bit IQS expression END.  None of the 8-bit
!     bytes in G are all 1's.
!   If the complete string begins at LIST, write a program to fill in
!   the total price for each product in (DU, "96", 8).  For simplicity
!   of programming do repeated additions instead of decimal
!   multiplications.  Create the grand total also, and put it (DU,
!   "128", 8) in the pseudo accumulator 13.0 through 14.0 ($RM and
!   $FT)."
!
! THE PRINTED STATEMENTS are START to XW2 below, as printed, except:
!
!  * THE PAGE PRINTS THE LABEL "LCON" TWICE, on "LX, $2, XW2" and on
!    the LCV under it, and "B, LCON" at the end of the loop.  The loop
!    must return to the LCV (returning to the LX would start the list
!    again), so the second is LCON2 here and the branch is B, LCON2.
!    That is the deck's reading; the ink has LCON on both lines.
!  * ' comments are written !'.
!
! READINGS WORTH RECORDING:
!  * "128-18" is right, and is the same device as Problem 2.7's -18:
!    the converted count's last bit lands in bit 17 of $L, and LOAD
!    COUNT takes "bits 0-17 of the half-word" (Reference Manual printed
!    p.24).
!  * "+(D, 48, 8)" is printed SIGNED, though E is described (DU, 48,
!    8).  Not resolved here.
!  * "(IQSQ)DD(DU,24,8),ENDQ": Q closes the alphabetic field; comment
!    (d) is about the blanks.
!
! THE DATA is the deck's: two products, 3 at 125 cents and 2 at 40.
! FROM THE PROBLEM STATEMENT the totals are 375 and 80 cents and the
! grand total 455; the stored byte forms (zone bits) are not derived
! here, because nothing can be run against them yet.
!
! A SECOND REASON IT CANNOT RUN ON THIS ASSEMBLER: strap_asm assembles
! "DD(DU,48,8), 000125" as the BINARY integer 125, not as six decimal
! digit bytes.  That is an assembler finding with its own reproducer,
! repro_dd_decimal_mode.strap, and a section in docs/NEXT.md.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   Z, $FT
LCON    LX, $2, XW2
LCON2   LCV(DU, 24, 8)(V+I), 0.24+0.48($2),128-18    !'$R cleared too
        LC, $1, $L; BXCZ, NEXT                       !'binary count field
ADD     +(D, 48, 8),-0.48($2)
        CB, $1, ADD
NEXT    ST(DU, 64, 8) (V+I), 0.64($2), 16            !'store total into F
        ST(DU, 32, 8) (V+I), 0.32($2)
        M+(DU, 64, 4), $FT                           !'update grand total
        L(BU, 32), TESTW
        KF(BU, 24), 0($2),8                          !'test for end of string
        BAE, LAST
KOMF    KF(BU,24)(V+I), 0.8($2)                      !'test for beginning of new field
        BZAE, KOMF
MORE    V+I, $2, 1.0                                 !'bypass 64 more bits to new D field
        B, LCON2
LAST    L(DU, 64, 4), $FT
        ST(DU, 64, 8), $FT
        ST(DU, 64, 8), $RM, 64
HALT    BEW, $
TESTW   (IQSQ)DD(DU,24,8),ENDQ                       !'end mark for string
        DD(BU, 8, 8), (2)11111111                    !'beginning mark for field
XW2     XW, LIST+0.72, 0, $

        SLC, 1200.0
! product 1: item 07, "BOLTS ", 3 units at 000125 cents, remarks "OK"
LIST    DD(BU, 8, 8), (2)11111111
        DD(DU,16,8), 07
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),BOLTS Q
        DD(DU,24,8), 003
        DD(DU,48,8), 000125
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,16,8),OKQ
! product 2: item 12, "NUTS  ", 2 units at 000040 cents, remarks "END"
        DD(BU, 8, 8), (2)11111111
        DD(DU,16,8), 12
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),NUTS  Q
        DD(DU,24,8), 002
        DD(DU,48,8), 000040
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(DU,24,8),ENDQ
        END, START
